{"name":"Himalaya Sky","hex":"#7695c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Himalayas","blocks":[{"text":"The Himalayas, or Himalaya, is a mountain range in Asia separating the plains of the Indian subcontinent from the Tibetan Plateau. The range has some of the highest peaks on Earth, including the highest, Mount Everest. More than 100 peaks exceeding elevations of 7,200 metres above sea level lie in the Himalayas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Himalayas_and_allied_ranges_NASA_Landsat_showing_the_eight_thousanders%2C_annotated_with_major_rivers.jpg/330px-Himalayas_and_allied_ranges_NASA_Landsat_showing_the_eight_thousanders%2C_annotated_with_major_rivers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Himalayas","wikidata":"Q5451"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Himalaya_annotated.jpg/500px-Himalaya_annotated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Himalaya_annotated.jpg/500px-Himalaya_annotated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHimalaya_annotated.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Panorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg/500px-Panorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Panorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg/1280px-Panorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Panorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg/500px-Panorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanorama_from_poonhill-2019-BJ.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Panorama_of_Himalayas_from_Ranikhet%2C_Uttarakhand%2C_India.jpg/500px-Panorama_of_Himalayas_from_Ranikhet%2C_Uttarakhand%2C_India.jp